        on the committed MW curve + published halo tracers (DOOR 5 / H048 / H038)
============================================================================================
  r_M(MW) = 10.21 kpc  (G072/L258, M_b = 7e10, a0 = 9.3619e-11)
  3 r_M   = 30.63 kpc   <- the KILL radius (any gamma steeper than -2.05 there)
  prediction P-A: gamma = -2.00 +- 0.02 constant, 20-100 kpc, no concentration;
                  NFW gamma moves 0.56 over the range, framework 0.12;
                  framework-NFW cross at 19 kpc.

============================================================================================
PART 1 -- THE EXACT MAPPING FROM THE CURVE TO gamma, AND THE CURVE-SPACE PREDICTION
============================================================================================
  M(<r)     = r v_c(r)^2 / G            (spherical)
  d ln M    = 2 d ln v_c + d ln r       ->  d ln M/d ln r = 2 alpha + 1
  rho(r)    = (1/4 pi r^2) dM/dr
  gamma     = d ln rho/d ln r = d ln M/d ln r - 3 = 2 d ln v_c/d ln r - 2   [G157-1]
  CHECK: for v_c = const (alpha = 0): gamma = -2 exactly (M~r, rho~r^-2).
         for v_c ~ r^-1/2 (Keplerian): gamma = -3   |  v_c ~ r^-0.05: gamma = -2.10
         for v_c ~ r^+0.01:            gamma = -1.98
  numeric closure on rho~r^-2 (analytic M = 4 pi A r): alpha_fit = +0.000000, gamma_fit = -2.000000, gamma_direct = -2.0
  [PASS] C1 [MAPPING] gamma = 2 d ln v_c/d ln r - 2 is the exact curve-to-density mapping; a r^-2 density gives alpha = 0 and gamma = -2 exactly
         measured: analytic rho~r^-2: alpha = +0.000000, gamma = -2.000000
         threshold: |gamma_fit + 2| < 1e-12.  rho = A r^-2 integrates to M = 4 pi A r exactly, so v_c = sqrt(G M/r) is exactly constant: alpha = 0, gamma = -2.  This is the algebraic identity the test operates on: gamma = 2 alpha - 2, so the -2.00 floor IS a flat rotation curve in v_c space.

  THE PREDICTION IN CURVE SPACE (P-A): v_c = const x r^{0.00 +- 0.01}
    over 20 -> 100 kpc the curve may change by at most [0.9840, 1.0162] x its 20-kpc value  (-1.6% .. +1.6%)
    a curve falling by more than 4% over the decade is past the -2.05 kill line
    kill line gamma = -2.05 <=> alpha = -0.025 <=> a 3.9% drop 20->100 kpc
  [PASS] C2 [CURVE-SPACE STATEMENT] P-A = a flat rotation curve to +-1% per e-folding (flat-plus); the kill line is a 3.9% total drop over 20-100 kpc
         measured: band [0.9840, 1.0162]; kill drop 3.9%

